        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0684" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg562"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ryan to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 10, 1889</date>.
                        (Received June 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Nothing further having reached this
                    legation concerning the case of Leon McLeod Baldwin, cruelly murdered in Durango
                    in August, 1887, since Mr. Whitehouse, acting under instructions of the
                    Department, <pb facs="0685" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/> on December 17 last, again
                    called Mr. Mariscal’s attention to the matter, I have deemed it my duty to renew
                    the solicitations for a humane and equitable adjustment of the case.</p>
                <p>Mr. Whitehouse in his dispatch, No. 218, of December 17, 1888, stated that Mr.
                    Mariscal asserted that he was not yet in possession of sufficient evidence to
                    form a definite opinion.</p>
                <p>It would certainly appear that since that time, nearly six months ago, Mr.
                    Mariscal had had ample time and opportunities to convince himself in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Ryan</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d248-a1.xml" xpointer="d248-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
